{"timestamp":"2025-12-08T10:56:45.723463","level":"info","event":"Done. Returned value was: [{'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503374, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=237735', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765191311, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Price Alert: 4 Critical Factors That Could Spark the Next Big Move This Week', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/bitcoin-price-critical-factors-week/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Bitcoin Price Alert: 4 Critical Factors That Could Spark the Next Big Move This Week Bitcoin traders are on high alert this week as several major market forces converge. The Bitcoin price faces a pivotal moment, caught between technical resistance and fundamental economic events. According to analysis from Cointelegraph, four specific factors could determine whether we see a bullish breakout or further consolidation. Let’s break down what every investor needs to watch. Can Bitcoin Price Smash Through the $90,000 Wall? The first and most immediate challenge is technical. The Bitcoin price has struggled to break and hold above resistance in the low $90,000s. This level acts like a ceiling, where selling pressure has consistently overwhelmed buying momentum. Each failed attempt weakens bullish sentiment, but a successful break could trigger significant upward movement. Traders are watching volume closely; a high-volume breakout would be more convincing than a thin, speculative push. How Will the Federal Reserve’s Decision Impact Crypto? This week’s U.S. Federal Reserve interest rate decision is the macro-economic wildcard. Higher rates typically strengthen the dollar, which can pressure risk assets like Bitcoin. However, the market has already priced in certain expectations. The key will be the Fed’s forward guidance and tone. A dovish shift, hinting at future rate cuts, could be the catalyst that injects fresh optimism and liquidity into the cryptocurrency market, potentially lifting the Bitcoin price . Therefore, crypto investors should listen for clues about inflation control and economic outlook. The reaction in traditional bond and equity markets will also provide immediate signals for Bitcoin’s likely direction. Is History Repeating? The 2022 Seasonal Pattern Echo Seasonal analysis suggests the current market structure might mirror the bottoming pattern seen in 2022. That period was characterized by: Prolonged consolidation after a major downturn Declining volatility and investor fatigue A gradual building of momentum that many dismissed If this analogy holds, the current phase could be the quiet before a sustained upward trend. While history doesn’t repeat exactly, these rhythms often rhyme, offering a valuable context for the current Bitcoin price action. Why Low Leverage Could Be a Secret Bullish Signal Paradoxically, low leverage and open interest in Bitcoin derivatives markets might be good news. After a period of liquidation, a reset in futures and options data indicates a healthier market foundation. Here’s why this matters: Reduced Systemic Risk: Lower leverage means fewer forced liquidations during volatility. Room for Growth: It shows speculators have been flushed out, allowing for organic buying to return. Sustainable Moves: Price increases from this point are less likely to be artificial pump-and-dump schemes. This reset could provide the stable base needed for a genuine, longer-term Bitcoin price recovery. The Verdict: A Week of High-Stakes Watchfulness This week presents a confluence of technical, fundamental, and cyclical factors for Bitcoin. The battle at the $90k resistance zone, interpreted through the lens of the Fed’s policy and against the backdrop of washed-out derivatives data, creates a high-stakes environment. The seasonal pattern adds an intriguing layer of historical context. Successful navigation of these elements could set the tone for the Bitcoin price trajectory for the coming quarter. Traders should prepare for potential volatility but also recognize the building blocks for a more sustainable rally. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Q: Why is the $90,000 level so important for Bitcoin right now? A: It’s a major technical resistance level where previous rallies have failed. A clean break above it on high volume would signal strong buyer conviction and could open the path to new highs. Q: How quickly does Bitcoin typically react to Fed rate decisions? A: The reaction is often immediate, occurring within hours of the announcement as traders digest the news. However, the full impact on trend can unfold over several days. Q: What does ‘low open interest’ in derivatives actually mean? A: It means fewer total outstanding futures and options contracts exist. This generally indicates less speculative activity and can lead to a more stable market less prone to violent liquidations. Q: Should I buy Bitcoin before or after the Fed decision? A: There’s no guaranteed answer. Some traders wait for the volatility of the announcement to pass, while others position beforehand based on their expectations. Your decision should align with your risk tolerance and strategy. Q: Is the comparison to 2022’s market bottom reliable? A> It’s a useful analytical tool, not a guarantee. Market cycles share similarities, but each one has unique drivers. Use it as one perspective among many in your analysis. Found this breakdown of critical Bitcoin price factors helpful? Share this article with your network on Twitter or LinkedIn to help other traders stay informed this week. Knowledge is power, especially in the fast-moving crypto markets. To learn more about the latest Bitcoin trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Bitcoin price action and institutional adoption. This post Bitcoin Price Alert: 4 Critical Factors That Could Spark the Next Big Move This Week first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BITCOIN|BLOCKCHAIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Market Analysis|trading.', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1765191338, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1765190574, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503323, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=874698', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765191048, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/55503323.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Binance receives full licenses from Abu Dhabi’s FSRA to operate its businesses', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Nellius Irene', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/binance-becomes-fully-licensed-in-abu-dhabi/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'On Monday, based on a news release and announcement from Binance, the Financial Services Regulatory Authority (FSRA) approved three licenses for Binance’s Nest Exchange Limited, Nest Clearing and Custody Limited, and Nest Trading Limited. Nest Services Limited, which will be renamed Nest Exchange Limited, has been approved as a recognized investment exchange with permission to run a multilateral trading facility. It will host the exchange’s business, including spot and derivatives markets. Nest Clearing and Custody Limited has been approved as a recognized clearing house with added custody and securities depository permissions, putting it in charge of clearing, settlement, and safekeeping of digital assets. A third entity, BCI Limited, set to become Nest Trading Limited, holds a broker-dealer license that covers dealing and arranging in investments, asset management, custody arrangements, and money services. Richard Teng, the co-CEO of Binance, declined to say whether Abu Dhabi is now Binance’s global headquarters when asked by reporters. “But for all intents and purposes, if you look at the regulatory sphere, I think the global regulators are more concerned with where we are regulated on a global basis,” he said, adding that Abu Dhabi Global Market is where his crypto exchange’s “global platform” will be governed. Regulatory milestone strengthens Binance’s global compliance push For Binance , the approval by ADGM represents a strategic pivot toward full compliance and institutional legitimacy . According to the company’s co-CEO, the FSRA license provides regulatory clarity and legitimacy, enabling Binance to support its global operations from ADGM. “While our global operations remain distributed, leveraging talent and innovation worldwide, this regulatory foundation offers our users peace of mind knowing Binance operates under a globally recognised, gold standard framework,” he said Regulators and officials see such licensing, along with the arrival of major global exchanges, as a confirmation of their progressive crypto-regulatory approaches. Binance lauded the FSRA’s forward-thinking approach, which safeguards users while fostering innovation. For the larger region, the decision supports ADGM’s bid to position Abu Dhabi as a leading global hub for regulated cryptocurrency trading and digital-asset services. New licensing framework positions Abu Dhabi as a rising crypto hub Binance does not own an official corporate headquarters, so it is not subject to certain tax rules. According to guidance from the FSRA, entities that are permitted to operate regulated activities in the ADGM must have their “mind and management” within the zone, which encompasses all commercial, governance, compliance, surveillance, operations, technical, IT, and human resources functions. Binance users enjoy further consumer protections and enhanced regulation through being subject to ADGM’s financial services framework, it says. Binance expects to start regulated operations on January 5, 2026. In an X post on Monday, Teng described this as an “important milestone for Binance,” noting that the company has become the first global exchange to secure regulatory approval from a respected regulator, enabling end-to-end supervision of its international operations and liquidity. The crypto platform already has a presence in the UAE, having held a virtual asset service provider license in Dubai since April 2024 and received a $2 billion investment from Abu Dhabi-based AI and technology venture firm MGX in March. Want your project in front of crypto’s top minds? Feature it in our next industry report, where data meets impact.', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|AED|BNB', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1765191244, 'UPDATED_ON': 1765191245, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1765190583, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 74, 'NAME': 'BNB', 'CATEGORY': 'BNB'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503189, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=237731', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765191011, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Real-World Asset Tokenization: How US Treasurys Are Fueling a Financial Revolution', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/real-world-asset-tokenization-us-treasurys/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Real-World Asset Tokenization: How US Treasurys Are Fueling a Financial Revolution Imagine a world where traditional financial assets like government bonds seamlessly integrate with blockchain technology. According to a recent report from crypto asset manager CoinShares, this future is rapidly approaching. The firm predicts that real-world asset tokenization , particularly of US Treasurys, will become the dominant force driving market growth by 2026. But what exactly does this mean for investors and the broader financial landscape? Why Is Real-World Asset Tokenization Gaining Momentum? The concept of real-world asset tokenization involves converting physical or traditional financial assets into digital tokens on a blockchain. CoinShares’ 2026 digital asset outlook reveals explosive growth in this sector, with on-chain US Treasurys more than doubling in value from $3.9 billion to $8.6 billion in just one year. This remarkable expansion signals a fundamental shift in how institutional players view blockchain technology. Several key factors are driving this adoption: Global demand for secure US dollar yields Superior efficiency of blockchain payment infrastructure Increasing regulatory recognition of blockchain reliability Growing institutional participation from traditional finance How Are US Treasurys Leading the Tokenization Charge? US government bonds have emerged as the unexpected champion of real-world asset tokenization . When yields remain secure and risks appear manageable, investors increasingly prefer tokenized Treasurys over alternatives like stablecoins. This preference creates a powerful feedback loop: as more institutions tokenize these assets, liquidity improves, attracting even more participants to the ecosystem. CoinShares emphasizes that this trend isn’t temporary. The firm expects tokenized Treasurys to continue leading the real-world asset tokenization market through 2026 and beyond. Established financial institutions are already issuing these digital assets, while regulators gradually acknowledge blockchain as legitimate financial infrastructure. What Benefits Does Tokenization Offer Traditional Finance? The advantages of real-world asset tokenization extend far beyond simple digitization. Blockchain technology introduces unprecedented transparency, reduces settlement times from days to minutes, and enables fractional ownership of high-value assets. These improvements could democratize access to investment opportunities previously reserved for large institutions. Consider these transformative benefits: 24/7 Market Access: Trade tokenized assets anytime, unlike traditional markets Reduced Costs: Eliminate intermediaries and associated fees Enhanced Liquidity: Fractional ownership allows smaller investment amounts Improved Transparency: All transactions recorded on immutable ledgers What Challenges Must Tokenization Overcome? Despite the promising growth of real-world asset tokenization , significant hurdles remain. Regulatory frameworks continue evolving, with different jurisdictions taking varied approaches to digital assets. Additionally, traditional financial institutions must overcome cultural resistance to blockchain adoption and ensure robust security measures protect these new digital assets. Interoperability between different blockchain networks presents another challenge. For real-world asset tokenization to reach its full potential, tokenized assets must move seamlessly across various platforms and ecosystems. Standardization efforts are underway, but widespread adoption requires coordinated industry action. The Future of Real-World Asset Tokenization CoinShares’ projection for 2026 suggests we’re witnessing just the beginning of a major financial transformation. As more traditional assets undergo real-world asset tokenization , we can expect increased innovation in financial products and services. The convergence of traditional finance and blockchain technology promises to create more inclusive, efficient, and transparent markets. This evolution represents more than technological advancement—it signals a fundamental reimagining of asset ownership and transfer. The success of tokenized US Treasurys provides a blueprint for how other asset classes might transition to blockchain platforms, potentially revolutionizing everything from real estate to intellectual property rights. Frequently Asked Questions What exactly is real-world asset tokenization? Real-world asset tokenization is the process of converting physical or traditional financial assets into digital tokens on a blockchain. These tokens represent ownership or rights to the underlying asset and can be traded or transferred like cryptocurrencies. Why are US Treasurys particularly suitable for tokenization? US Treasurys offer stable yields, high liquidity, and perceived safety. Their tokenization combines these traditional benefits with blockchain advantages like 24/7 trading, reduced settlement times, and accessibility to global investors. How does tokenization benefit everyday investors? Tokenization enables fractional ownership, allowing smaller investors to access assets previously requiring large capital outlays. It also increases market transparency and reduces intermediary costs that typically eat into returns. Is real-world asset tokenization regulated? Regulation is evolving globally. Many jurisdictions are developing frameworks specifically for tokenized assets, with increasing recognition of blockchain as legitimate financial infrastructure. What risks are associated with tokenized assets? Potential risks include smart contract vulnerabilities, regulatory uncertainty, platform security issues, and market liquidity challenges during early adoption phases. Which other assets might be tokenized next? Beyond government bonds, real estate, commodities, private equity, and intellectual property represent promising candidates for future tokenization as the technology matures and regulatory clarity improves. Found this insight into the future of finance valuable? Share this article with colleagues and friends interested in how blockchain technology is transforming traditional assets. The revolution in real-world asset tokenization affects everyone in the financial ecosystem. To learn more about the latest cryptocurrency trends, explore our article on key developments shaping institutional adoption and blockchain innovation. This post Real-World Asset Tokenization: How US Treasurys Are Fueling a Financial Revolution first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BLOCKCHAIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Finance|Investment|Tokenization', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1765191015, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1765190574, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 49, 'NAME': 'TECHNOLOGY', 'CATEGORY': 'TECHNOLOGY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503197, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=460924', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765190931, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/52/55503197.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Harvard Bets Big on Bitcoin With $443M Stake, Outpacing Gold 2-to-1', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Anas Hassan', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/harvard-bets-big-on-bitcoin-with-443m-stake-outpacing-gold-2-to-1/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': 'Harvard University expanded its Bitcoin ETF holdings by 257% in the third quarter, making the iShares Bitcoin Trust its largest disclosed position with $442.8 million as of September 30. According to Matt Hougan , Bitwise CIO, Harvard simultaneously increased its gold ETF holdings by 99% to $235 million, allocating to Bitcoin at a 2-to-1 ratio relative to gold. Harvard ramped its bitcoin investment in Q3 from $117m ot $443m. It also boosted its gold ETF allocation from $102m to $235m. Think about that for a second: Harvard decided to put on a debasement trade and it allocated to bitcoin 2-to-1 over gold. — Matt Hougan (@Matt_Hougan) December 8, 2025 The $443 million position represents approximately 0.75% of Harvard’s $57 billion endowment, ranking the institution among the top 20 largest holders of the BlackRock-managed fund . Timing Proves Problematic as Bitcoin Tumbles Harvard’s aggressive Bitcoin accumulation came right before a sharp market correction that has erased substantial value from its cryptocurrency holdings. Bitcoin has dropped more than 20% since the third quarter ended, falling from $114,000 to around $92,000. Source: TradingView The timing suggests Harvard could face a 14% loss on its third-quarter purchases in the best-case scenario, assuming shares were bought at July’s low point, which represents an $89 million paper loss on the recent position alone. While the losses remain a fraction of Harvard’s massive endowment, the university’s annualized returns have lagged behind some Ivy League peers over the past decade, according to WSJ . Harvard posted an 8.2% return ranking ninth out of 10 elite schools in a Markov Processes International comparison. For the year ending June 30, Harvard reported an 11.9% gain but trailed MIT’s 14.8% and Stanford’s 14.3%. Stanford finance professor Joshua Rauh explained in an interview with The Harvard Crimson that “ investors often seem to view both bitcoin and gold as hedges against a collapse of the international monetary system in general, and against a loss of the US dollar in particular. ” However, he cautioned that “ the extent to which either actually protects investors from these forces is uncertain and scenario-dependent. “ Academic Skepticism Meets Institutional Validation Harvard’s substantial Bitcoin allocation stands in stark contrast to earlier predictions from its own economics faculty. Kenneth Rogoff, a Harvard professor and former IMF chief economist, stated in 2018 that Bitcoin would more likely trade at $100 than $100,000 within a decade. “ I think bitcoin will be worth a tiny fraction of what it is now if we’re headed out 10 years from now, ” Rogoff told CNBC, arguing that removing money laundering and tax evasion would leave Bitcoin with “ very small ” transaction uses. Rogoff recently acknowledged his misjudgment in his new book “ Our Dollar, Your Problem, ” writing, “I was far too optimistic about the US coming to its senses about sensible cryptocurrency regulation.” Harvard economist @krogoff admits his $100 Bitcoin crash prediction was wrong as $BTC trades above $115,000. #Bitcoin #Harvard https://t.co/AX8l7Aitxz — Cryptonews.com (@cryptonews) August 20, 2025 He added that he “ did not anticipate a situation where regulators, and especially the regulator in chief, would be able to brazenly hold hundreds of millions (if not billions) of dollars in cryptocurrencies seemingly without consequence given the blatant conflict of interest. “ Despite growing institutional adoption, criticism of Harvard’s Bitcoin investment has intensified. MarketWatch columnist Brett Arends called the investment an “ environmental catastrophe, ” noting that Bitcoin’s global computing network uses more energy than Thailand or Poland annually. Meanwhile, Stanford professor Darrell Duffie also expressed surprise at the investment, stating, “ Bitcoin does not pay dividends and has limited uses as a payment instrument. “ Bitcoin’s Path Forward Remains Uncertain Bitcoin is struggling to find direction amid ETF outflows and weakening market sentiment , creating uncertainty about whether it can reclaim the $100,000 threshold. More than $2.7 billion has left Bitcoin ETF products over the past five weeks. Speaking with Cryptonews, Arthur Azizov, Founder and Investor at B2 Ventures, described the current situation as “ a market that has lost its anchor at the exact moment it needed stability. “ He noted a disconnect with traditional markets, pointing out that “ the S&P 500 is up more than 16% this year, while Bitcoin is down about 3%. “ Azizov identified key resistance levels ahead, explaining that “ a large share of Bitcoin is currently held at a loss, so each move toward $96,000–$100,000 meets selling from holders who want to exit at break-even. ” He added that approximately $3.35 billion in Bitcoin options expire around a $91,000 area of interest, making traders cautious. “ Only a strong move above $100,000 could flip the script, restore confidence, and open the way toward $120,000+ level, ” Azizov stated. “ If that fails, a deeper pullback to the broad $82,000–$88,000 zone may be needed to attempt to break the $100k ceiling once again. “ The post Harvard Bets Big on Bitcoin With $443M Stake, Outpacing Gold 2-to-1 appeared first on Cryptonews .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin News|Bitcoin|Bitcoin ETF', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1765191023, 'UPDATED_ON': 1765191024, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1765190582, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1680604053}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503195, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=460967', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765190906, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/52/55503195.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'British Columbia Seizes $1M in Cash and Gold Linked to QuadrigaCX Co-Founder', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Amin Ayan', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/british-columbia-seizes-1m-in-cash-and-gold-linked-to-quadrigacx-co-founder/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': 'British Columbia has secured a landmark victory under its unexplained wealth order (UWO) regime, after the province successfully seized more than $1 million in cash, gold and luxury items tied to QuadrigaCX co-founder Michael Patryn. Key Takeaways: B.C. seized over $1M in cash, gold and luxury items tied to QuadrigaCX co-founder Michael Patryn. Police found 45 gold bars, high-end watches and a loaded pistol in Patryn’s safety deposit box. Authorities allege the assets came from misappropriated QuadrigaCX customer funds. The Supreme Court of British Columbia granted the forfeiture after Patryn chose not to contest the action, clearing the way for authorities to liquidate 45 gold bars, multiple high-end watches and roughly $250,000 in cash originally seized during an RCMP investigation. The order marks one of the most significant applications of the province’s new anti–money laundering tools. Gold Bars, Rolexes and a .45 Pistol Found in Patryn’s Safety Deposit Box Court filings show the seized items were discovered in a CIBC safety deposit box in Vancouver in 2021, including three one-kilogram gold bars and 42 smaller bars. Officers also recovered Rolex and Chanel watches, rings, jewelry, identification documents, and even a Ruger 1911 .45-caliber pistol with loaded magazines. At current prices, the gold alone is valued at more than $800,000. The civil forfeiture office alleged the assets were purchased using QuadrigaCX customer funds, money that investigators say was misappropriated during the years leading up to the exchange’s infamous collapse. QUADRIGACX CO-FOUNDER FACES UNEXPLAINED WEALTH COURT ORDER Michael Patryn, co-founder of QuadrigaCX and known as \"Sifu\" in the DeFi community, is facing a new court order in British Columbia which requires him to explain how he acquired his assets. QuadrigaCX collapsed in… pic.twitter.com/3N6mEkYfjp — Crypto Town Hall (@Crypto_TownHall) March 28, 2024 The unexplained wealth order required Patryn to demonstrate legitimate sources for the assets, but while he initially challenged the investigation on constitutional grounds, he ultimately withdrew his response and did not appear when the province sought judgment. QuadrigaCX, once Canada’s largest cryptocurrency exchange, imploded in 2019 after CEO Gerald Cotten died in India and it emerged that more than $169 million in customer assets were missing. Regulators later concluded that the platform had effectively become a Ponzi scheme by 2016, with new deposits used to fulfill withdrawal requests while Cotten allegedly siphoned funds to finance personal expenses. Patryn’s Criminal Past Resurfaces in QuadrigaCX Forfeiture Case Investigators have long alleged that Patryn, also known by several aliases including Omar Dhanani, played a central role in the exchange’s operations and benefited from client funds. His criminal history was cited in the forfeiture filings. In 2005, under the name Omar Dhanani, he was convicted in the US for operating an online identity-theft and money-laundering service and later deported to Canada. The province’s win now triggers a separate review to determine whether any of the recovered assets can be directed to compensate QuadrigaCX creditors. Claimants received just 13 cents on the dollar when bankruptcy proceedings concluded in May 2023. Patryn’s current whereabouts remain uncertain, though the civil forfeiture suit lists his last known location as Thailand. In 2023, QuadrigaCX announced plans to start the “interim distribution” of funds to creditors, despite only a fraction of the missing funds being recovered. The post British Columbia Seizes $1M in Cash and Gold Linked to QuadrigaCX Co-Founder appeared first on Cryptonews .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Blockchain News|Bitcoin|Gold|Regulation', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1765191023, 'UPDATED_ON': 1765191023, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1765190582, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1680604053}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503059, 'GUID': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/bloomberg-analyst-mike-mcglone-releases-year-end-bitcoin-btc-forecast-he-gives-two-levels/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765190769, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/55503059.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bloomberg Analyst Mike McGlone Releases Year-End Bitcoin (BTC) Forecast! He Gives Two Levels!', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Elif Azra Güven', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/bloomberg-analyst-mike-mcglone-releases-year-end-bitcoin-btc-forecast-he-gives-two-levels/', 'SOURCE_ID': 81, 'BODY': \"Bitcoin (BTC) started the critical week where the FED will announce its interest rate decision for December above $91,000. Bitcoin, which fell below $90,000 over the weekend, has recovered slightly, but expectations of a decline continue. Stating that Bitcoin could fall to $50,000 at this point, Bloomberg Intelligence senior commodity strategist Mike McGlone shared his new analysis. Mike McGlone stated that $94,000-$84,000 is very critical for Bitcoin and predicted that Bitcoin is more likely to finish 2025 below $84,000. McGlone emphasized that Bitcoin's average of its yearly highs from 2021-23 and its lows in 2024 is around $50,100, and a drop to that level is still a possible scenario. Pointing out that there is currently no data to stop this decline, the analyst predicts that BTC could lead to the next recession. While Bitcoin has reached millions of dollars today and led the way for riskier assets in 2009, it could also lead to a comeback, according to the analyst. While McGlone expects Bitcoin to decline overall, he added that if Bitcoin achieves a positive trend above around $94,000 within the year, it would signal a recovery in the overall market. As you may recall, Mike McGlone argued that Bitcoin could experience a serious bear market in the near future and decline to $10,000. According to the analyst, such an extreme bearish scenario could be possible if the macroeconomic stress and structural weakness in BTC and cryptocurrencies continue. McGlone stated that this is the worst-case scenario, adding that a BTC drop to $50,000 due to weakening market sentiment is a more realistic scenario. *This is not investment advice. Continue Reading: Bloomberg Analyst Mike McGlone Releases Year-End Bitcoin (BTC) Forecast! He Gives Two Levels!\", 'KEYWORDS': 'Analysis|Bitcoin|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1765190784, 'UPDATED_ON': 1765190784, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 81, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinsistemi', 'NAME': 'BitcoinSistemi', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1765190562, 'CREATED_ON': 1692873798, 'UPDATED_ON': 1764762589}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 55503057, 'GUID': 'https://timestabloid.com/?p=91677', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1765190720, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Latest Crypto Updates: Cheems and Pudgy Penguins Rise, $APEING Surges as the Best Crypto to Watch Today With Explosive Gains', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'PR Desk', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/latest-crypto-updates-cheems-and-pudgy-penguins-rise-apeing/', 'SOURCE_ID': 67, 'BODY': 'The crypto universe never sleeps, and the race for the next explosive coin i